---
description: Use when comparing pi-rust with upstream pi, porting an upstream commit, or answering what pi-rust is missing
alwaysApply: false
---

Read @docs/parity/README.md and @docs/parity/GAPS.md first.

- Find gaps with `cargo xtask parity --upstream <upstream-checkout>` and check each finding in both codebases before acting on it.
- Port one upstream commit per change and name it in the commit message: `fix(scope): <what> (upstream <sha>)`, with the 9-character SHA.
- Record accepted differences in `docs/parity/allowlist.json` with a reason, and open gaps in `docs/parity/GAPS.md`.
- When the port is complete up to a commit, move `syncedCommit`, `syncedVersion`, and `syncedOn` in `docs/parity/upstream.json`.
